---
import Screenshot from "../Screenshot.astro";
import Window from "../Window.astro";
---

<section aria-labelledby="code-title" class="scheme-dark overflow-hidden py-20 sm:py-28">
  <div class="container-page">
    <div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-16">
      <div class="lg:col-span-6">
        <p class="text-eyebrow">Design in code</p>
        <h2 id="code-title" class="text-heading mt-4">Make it look exactly like your website.</h2>
        <p class="text-lead mt-6">
          The default design looks good with just your logo and color. When you want more, every page of your careers
          site is HTML, CSS, and Liquid templates you can change.
        </p>
      </div>
      <ul class="check-list flex flex-col gap-4 self-end text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed lg:col-span-5 lg:col-start-8">
        <li>Edit right in Emploist, with a live preview at desktop and phone sizes.</li>
        <li>
          Or download the code, change it in your own editor or with an AI assistant, and preview it on your computer
          with a single command.
        </li>
        <li>Mistakes are caught before you save, so candidates always see a working page.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <Window class="mt-14 sm:mt-16">
      <Screenshot
        name="careers-code"
        scheme="dark"
        alt="The careers page code editor in Emploist: the layout template with syntax highlighting on the left, and a live preview of the careers page on the right."
        sizes="(min-width: 76rem) 72rem, calc(100vw - 2.5rem)"
      />
    </Window>
  </div>
</section>
